{{Quote|Careful we must be. Deserted this planet was, long ago, after many wars.|Yoda|<ref name="Sacrifice" />}}
'''Moraband''', known in antiquity as '''Korriban''', was an [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] [[planet]] that was [[Homeworld|home]] to the ancient [[Sith]] Order. The [[Desert|desolate]] and [[mountain]]ous world was abandoned after many ancient wars. The [[Valley of the Dark Lords]] on the planet's surface was the final resting place of [[Darth Bane]], the [[Sith Lord]] who created the [[Rule of Two]]. During the [[Clone Wars]], [[Yoda]] [[Mission to Moraband|ventured]] to the abandoned world as part of his journey to discover the [[Force spirit|secrets]] of [[Immortality|eternal consciousness]].

==Description==
{{Quote|Known long ago as Korriban, this ancient homeworld of the Sith was abandoned after countless wars transformed it into an infertile wasteland.|Darth Sidious, ''The Secrets of the Sith''|<ref name="SotS">''[[Star Wars: The Secrets of the Sith]]''</ref>}}
[[File:Moraband-Sacrifice.png|thumb|right|250px|The desolate Moraband landscape]]
A [[Planet|world]] of [[mountain]]s and [[Color|red]] sands, Moraband was abandoned after widespread devastation during numerous wars.<ref name="Sacrifice" /> Located on the surface was the [[Valley of the Dark Lords]],<ref name="Databank" /> a [[Desert|wasteland]] filled with the tombs of ancient [[Dark Lord of the Sith|Dark Lords of the Sith]] such as [[Darth Bane]], among others.<ref name="Sacrifice" />

==History==
===Early history===
{{Quote|They are the Despoilers of Worlds, and have Laid to Waste once Fertile Habitats such as Korriban, Ziost, Ixigul, Asog, and Others.|Kli the Elder, ''Rammahgon''|<ref name="TROS Junior Novel">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: A Junior Novel]]''</ref>}}
[[File:Valley_of_the_Dark_Lords_TCW.png|thumb|left|250px|Sith temples and monuments were constructed on Korriban during the time of the ancient Sith.]]
Around [[5000 BBY]],<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> a [[Unidentified rogue Jedi|rogue member]] of the [[Jedi Order]] founded the [[Sith]], a group of [[Dark side of the Force|dark side]] users. After they were denounced by the Jedi Order,<ref name="SWE Sith">{{SWE|groups|sith|Sith}}</ref> the Sith went on a long and arduous search across [[the galaxy]] for a new [[homeworld]], until they reached a [[star system]] inhabited by worshippers of the dark side, who greeted them as demigods and made them their rulers. Although they also settled on other planets in the system, such as [[Ziost]], the Sith chose the planet then known as Korriban, later to be renamed Moraband, to erect their mausoleums, making it their true spiritual sanctuary and the epicenter of their dark powers.<ref name="Mustafar and Other Outer Rim Planets" /> As mentioned by the [[Jedi]] writer [[Kli the Elder]] in the ''[[Rammahgon]]'', the planet once had a fertile habitat, much like [[Exegol|Ixigul]] (or Exegol), Ziost, and [[Asog]], though the worlds fell to the dominion of the Sith<ref name="TROS Junior Novel" /> and Korriban was left an abandoned wasteland after their many wars. Despite this, its existence was never forgotten by the Sith.<ref name="Sacrifice" />

The planet stood as a sacred place of ceremonial rituals for the Sith. The [[burial]] ceremony of a Dark [[Lord]] of the Sith would be accompanied by hundreds of Sith warriors carrying the body of the fallen master. The corpse was stored in the tomb along with precious objects, and an escort of slaves accompanied the deceased on his journey to the spirit realm. The Sith then left the planet until the next burial.<ref name="Mustafar and Other Outer Rim Planets" /> [[Darth]] Bane, who created the [[Rule of Two]] a [[millennium]] before the rise of the [[Galactic Empire]], was the last Dark Lord to be buried at Moraband's Valley of the Dark Lords.<ref name="Bane SWE">{{SWE|characters|darth-bane|Darth Bane}}</ref> Meanwhile, the world fell into myth for the galaxy at large, much like [[Dromund Kaas]] did.<ref name="RiseFall">''[[Star Wars: The Rise and Fall of the Galactic Empire]]''</ref>

===Clone Wars===
{{Quote|Master Yoda has come to Moraband, although why, I do not know. We shall, however, use the strong bond that once existed between you and your master to allow us to see things that we otherwise could not.|Darth Sidious, to Darth Tyranus|<ref name="Sacrifice" />}}
[[File:YodasJediFighter-SWZ79.png|thumb|right|250px|Yoda arrives on Moraband in his custom Jedi starfighter.]]
During the [[Clone Wars]], [[Yoda]] was [[Mission to Moraband|sent]] to Moraband by the [[Force Priestesses]] as part of his journey to discover the [[Force spirit|secrets]] of [[Immortality|eternal consciousness]]. Once there, he encountered a number of Sith spirits, including that of Darth Bane himself. As he ventured further into the Valley of the Dark Lords, he encountered [[Force vision|visions]] created by [[Darth Sidious]], the reigning Dark Lord of the Sith who attempted to corrupt Yoda to help win the Clone Wars. The plan failed, and Yoda left Moraband behind.<ref name="Sacrifice" /> 

===Imperial Era and beyond===
{{Quote|Although the world itself may be dead, the spirits of the fallen Sith entombed in the Valley of the Dark Lords live on eternally. As my power grows, I have heard the whispers of my predecessors calling to me from Moraband, offering me their dark secrets. When the time comes, I shall answer.|Darth Sidious, ''The Secrets of the Sith''|<ref name="SotS" />}}
Before and after the [[Proclamation of the New Order]], Sidious traveled to the planet to learn from the spirits of the Dark Lords of the Sith.<ref name="Mustafar and Other Outer Rim Planets" /> During one of his first visits to Moraband, Sidious discovered and stole a huge [[Sith holocron (Grand Republic Medical Facility)|Sith holocron]], which he later stored in his secret lair in the [[Grand Imperial Medical Facility|Grand Republic Medical Facility]].<ref name="CL 2016">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref> During his other visits to Moraband, Sidious experienced visions of [[Sith Master]]s battling [[Sith apprentice]]s.<ref name="Disturbance">{{StoryCite|story=Disturbance|book=From a Certain Point of View: The Empire Strikes Back}}</ref> Some time after the [[Battle of Jakku|end]] of the [[Galactic Civil War]], [[Luke Skywalker]] traveled to Moraband to investigate about the Force.<ref name="The Dark Side">''[[Star Wars: The Dark Side]]''</ref>

[[File:SidiousReturns-TROS.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Darth Sidious believed he had heard his predecessors calling to him from Moraband.]]
During the [[First Order-Resistance War]], Sidious mentioned Moraband while chronicling Sith history in his book, ''[[The Secrets of the Sith]]''. He stated that he had heard his predecessors calling to him from Moraband on Exegol in the [[Unknown Regions]], offering him their dark secrets. Once the Sith Eternal's [[fleet]], the [[Final Order]], reclaimed Moraband, Sidious planned to answer.<ref name="SotS">''[[Star Wars: The Secrets of the Sith]]''</ref> Shortly afterward, however, Sidious was [[Death|destroyed]] along with the Sith fleet in the [[Battle of Exegol]].<ref name="Episode IX">{{Film|IX}}</ref> [[Historian]] [[Beaumont Kin]] uncovered references to Moraband during the [[Exegol Excavation Project]], proving the world did indeed exist and was not simply a myth.<ref name="RiseFall" />

==Locations==
{{Main|Valley of the Dark Lords}}
The Valley of the Dark Lords was an area of Moraband that contained numerous monuments serving as crypts for deceased Dark Lords of the Sith. The [[Sith temple (Valley of the Dark Lords)|largest monument]] in the valley housed the [[Tomb of Darth Bane|tomb]] of Darth Bane, the founder of the Rule of Two.<ref name="Sacrifice" />

===Sith temples===
{{Main|Sith temple (Sword of Khashyun)|Sith temple (Valley of the Dark Lords)}}
[[File:SithTempleMoraband-Sacrifice.png|thumb|left|250px|Sith temple entrance]]
The [[Sith temple]] was the largest monument in the Valley of the Dark Lords, a corridor of ancient monuments that serve as crypts for the Dark Lords of the Sith. It contained the tomb of Darth Bane, the Sith Lord who founded the Rule of Two, and a [[Moraband execution chamber|massive execution chamber]] that the ancient Sith used to sacrifice [[Jedi]] prisoners.<ref name="Databank" /> Another Sith [[Sith temple (Sword of Khashyun)|temple]] on Moraband was one that housed the [[Sword of Khashyun]]. The temple had many booby traps, giant [[Sentry (Moraband)|sentries]], and [[Tuk'ata|Sith hounds]] that protected the temple and the [[sword]].<ref name="GE 4" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:Korriban_Valley_TOR.jpg|thumb|right|300px|Concept art of Korriban for ''Star Wars: The Old Republic'']]
Moraband originated in the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity, where it was first mentioned, albeit indirectly, in the [[Tales of the Jedi – Dark Lords of the Sith 1|first issue]] of the [[Star Wars comic books|comic]] miniseries [[Star Wars: Tales of the Jedi – Dark Lords of the Sith|''Star Wars: Tales of the Jedi - Dark Lords of the Sith'']], which was written by [[Tom Veitch]] and [[Kevin J. Anderson]], and published by [[Dark Horse Comics]]<ref name="TJDLS 1">[[Tales of the Jedi – Dark Lords of the Sith 1|''Tales of the Jedi – Dark Lords of the Sith'' 1]]</ref> on [[October 1]], [[1994]].<ref name="TJDLS 1 date">{{DarkHorse|url=Comics/93-518/Star-Wars-Tales-of-the-Jedi---Dark-Lords-of-the-Sith-1-of-6|text=Star Wars: Tales of the Jedi - Dark Lords of the Sith #1 (of 6)}}</ref> It subsequently debuted in the [[Tales of the Jedi – Dark Lords of the Sith 2|following issue]], which was written by Veitch and Anderson, illustrated by [[Chris Gossett]], and published by Dark Horse<ref name="darklords2">[[Tales of the Jedi – Dark Lords of the Sith 2|''Tales of the Jedi – Dark Lords of the Sith'' 2]]</ref> on [[November 1]] of the same year.<ref name="TJDLS 2 date">{{DarkHorse|url=Comics/93-534/Star-Wars-Tales-of-the-Jedi---Dark-Lords-of-the-Sith-2-of-6|text=Star Wars: Tales of the Jedi - Dark Lords of the Sith #2 (of 6)}}</ref> The planet was initially known as "Korriban",<ref name="darklords2" /> a name coined by Anderson.<ref name="Veitch Interview">{{WebCite|url=https://www.starwarsunderworld.com/2016/08/interview-with-dark-empire-writer-tom.html|text=Interview with ''Dark Empire'' Writer Tom Veitch|work=Star Wars Underworld|archivedate=20200613234534}}</ref>

In the current ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]] continuity, the planet Moraband was first mentioned in "[[Destiny (The Clone Wars)|Destiny]]," an episode in the [[The Clone Wars: The Lost Missions|sixth season]] of the animated television series ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'', and made its first appearance in the following episode, "[[Sacrifice (episode)|Sacrifice]]." During the development of the episode the pre-established name "Korriban" was used for the planet. However, ''Star Wars'' creator [[George Lucas]] preferred the name "Moraband" and as such the planet was renamed to reflect his wishes.<ref name="Sacrifice Trivia">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/sacrifice-trivia-gallery|text="Sacrifice" Trivia Gallery}}</ref> The name "Korriban" was later reintroduced into canon as an ancient name for Moraband in "[[Gaze of Stone]]," a short story written by [[George Mann]] and published in the [[2019]] short story collection ''[[Myths & Fables]]''.<ref name="Gaze of Stone">{{StoryCite|story=Gaze of Stone|book=Myths & Fables}}</ref>

